Nāma"}}},"song":{"meta":{"page":73,"first_line":"emana durmati","author":"Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur"},"title":["Dainyātmikā"],"author":["by Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur"],"verses":[{"number":"1","text":["(prabhu he!)","emana durmati     saṁsāra bhitare","    paḍiyā āchhinu āmi","tava nija-jana      kona mahājane","    pāṭhāiyā dile tumi"],"translation":["O Lord! I am very wicked-minded and have fallen into this material world, but You have sent a great soul, Your associate (to rescue me)."],"isLong":false},{"number":"2","text":["dayā kari more    patita dekhiyā","    kahila āmāre giyā","ohe dīna-jana    śuna bhāla kathā","    ullasita ha’be hiyā"],"translation":["Seeing me so fallen and being merciful, he came to me and said, “O humble soul, listen to this wonderful message and your heart will rejoice."],"isLong":false},{"number":"3","text":["tomāre tārite    śrī-kṛṣṇa-chaitanya","    navadvīpe avatāra","tomā hena kata    dīna-hīna jane","    karilena bhava-pāra"],"translation":["“Śrī Kṛṣṇa Chaitanya has appeared in Nabadwīp to deliver you. He has brought many humble souls just like you to the shore of the ocean of material existence."],"isLong":false},{"number":"4","text":["vedera pratijñā    rākhibāra tare","    rukma-varṇa vipra-suta","mahāprabhu nāme    nadīyā mātāya","(mahāprabhu nāme    jagata mātāya)","    saṅge bhāi avadhūta"],"translation":["“To fulfil the prophecies of the Vedas, He has appeared with a golden complexion as a brāhmaṇ’s son bearing the name ‘Mahāprabhu’ and driven all of Nadia (all the world) mad with divine love in the company of His brother Nityānanda."],"isLong":false},{"number":"5","text":["nanda suta yini    chaitanya gosāñī","    nija-nāma kari’ dāna","tārila jagat    tumi-o yāiyā","    laha nija paritrāṇa"],"translation":["“Śrī Chaitanya, who is Kṛṣṇa Himself, has distributed His own Name and delivered the world. Go also and accept your deliverance.”"],"isLong":false},{"number":"6","text":["se kathā śuniyā    āsiyāchhi, nātha!","    tomāra charaṇa-tale","bhakati-vinoda    kā̐diyā kā̐diyā","    āpana-kāhinī bale"],"translation":["O Lord, hearing this message, Bhakti Vinod has come to the soles of Your feet. Crying, he tells his story."],"isLong":false}],"resources":{"audio":[{"title":"Srila B.R. Sridhar Dev-Goswami Maharaj","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/bharatimaharaj/sridhar-maharaj-and-govinda-7","personSlug":"srila-b-r-sridhar-dev-goswami-maharaj"},{"title":"Srila B.S. Govinda Dev-Goswami Maharaj","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/bharatimaharaj/govinda-maharaj-emona-durmati","personSlug":"srila-b-s-govinda-dev-goswami-maharaj"},{"title":"Nabadwip temple","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/bharatimaharaj/navadwip-scsm-emona-durmati","personSlug":"nabadwip-temple"},{"title":"Srila B.B. Avadhut Maharaj","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/bharatimaharaj/avadxut-maxaradzh-emona","personSlug":"srila-b-b-avadhut-maharaj"},{"title":"Srila B.B. Avadhut Maharaj","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/bharatimaharaj/avadxut-maxaradzh-emona-1","personSlug":"srila-b-b-avadhut-maharaj"},{"title":"Srila B.N. Acharya Maharaj","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/bharatimaharaj/acharya-maharaj-emona-durmati","personSlug":"srila-b-n-acharya-maharaj"},{"title":"Srila B.S. Goswami Maharaj","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/bharatimaharaj/goswami-maharaj-emona-durmati","personSlug":"srila-b-s-goswami-maharaj"},{"title":"Kamal Krishna Prabhu","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/jayasri-sound/08-emana-durmati","personSlug":"kamal-krishna-prabhu"},{"title":"Manasa Krishna Prabhu","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/huron/emona-durmati","personSlug":"manasa-krishna-prabhu"},{"title":"Caracas temple","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/bharatimaharaj/shchsm-karakas-emona-durmati","personSlug":"caracas-temple"},{"title":"Sudarshan Prabhu","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/bharatimaharaj/sudarshan-prabhu-dainyatmika","personSlug":"sudarshan-prabhu"}]},"hasWbw":false,"hasVersesText":true,"hasVersesTranslations":true,"hasLongVerses":false,"fullInlineWbw":false},"telegraphUrl":"https://telegra.ph/Dainyātmikā-02-22"},"head":{"canonical":"/en-pe/emona-durmati-samsara-bhitore/","description":"Dainyātmikā — a Vaiṣṇava song by Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur with lyrics, English translation and word-by-word meaning. From Pocket Kirtan Guide.","title":"Dainyātmikā. by Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur | Kirtan Site"},"kind":"song","route":{"kind":"item","bookId":"en-pe","slug":"emona-durmati-samsara-bhitore"}}